    <title>Cross-Attention Mechanisms in Vision-Language Models</title>
    <summary>We study cross-attention patterns in vision-language models and show that sparse attention achieves comparable performance to dense attention with significantly reduced memory usage and faster inference times on standard benchmarks.</summary>
    <author><name>Dave Brown</name></author>
    <author><name>Eve Green</name></author>
